  }</style><span class="" data-index="0" data-forhalf="★" style="position: relative; overflow: hidden; cursor: default; display: block; float: left; color: gray; font-size: 18px;">★</span><span class="" data-index="1" data-forhalf="★" style="position: relative; overflow: hidden; cursor: default; display: block; float: left; color: gray; font-size: 18px;">★</span><span class="" data-index="2" data-forhalf="★" style="position: relative; overflow: hidden; cursor: default; display: block; float: left; color: gray; font-size: 18px;">★</span><span class="" data-index="3" data-forhalf="★" style="position: relative; overflow: hidden; cursor: default; display: block; float: left; color: gray; font-size: 18px;">★</span><span class="" data-index="4" data-forhalf="★" style="position: relative; overflow: hidden; cursor: default; display: block; float: left; color: gray; font-size: 18px;">★</span><p role="status" style="position: absolute; left: -200rem;">0</p></div></div></div><div class="votes">0 votes</div></div></div><div class="item mobile-hidden"><div class="icon ui-tag"></div><div class="label">Prime Factorization,  Medium,  Math</div></div><div class="share-container"><div class="item share-item"><div class="icon ui-share"></div><div class="label">Share</div></div></div></div></div><div class="problem-tabs-container"><div class="problem-tabs"><div class="tab active" role="presentation">Details</div><a href="https://www.hackerearth.com/problem/algorithm/count-pairs-01cd4368/submissions/"><div class="tab" role="presentation">Submissions</div></a><a href="https://www.hackerearth.com/problem/algorithm/count-pairs-01cd4368/discussion/"><div class="tab" role="presentation">Discussion</div></a><a href="https://www.hackerearth.com/problem/algorithm/count-pairs-01cd4368/similar_problems/"><div class="tab" role="presentation">Similar Problems</div></a></div></div><div><div class="split-view"><div class="split-pane flex"><div class="pane-left"><div class="problem-details"><div class=""><div class="title">Problem</div><div class="description"><p>Given a number <strong>n</strong> you have to count number of <strong>pairs (x,y) such that x * y = n and gcd(x, y) = 1</strong></p>
<p><strong>Note:</strong> gcd(x, y) is the greatest number that divides both x and y.</p>
<p>Refer: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greatest_common_divisor">link</a>
</p>
<p>Use of Fast I/O is recommended.
</p>
<p><br>
</p>
<p><strong>Input format:</strong>
</p>
<p>First line consists of a number <strong>T</strong>, denoting number of test cases. </p>
<p>Each of the next <strong>T</strong> lines contains a single number <strong>N</strong>. </p>
<p><br>
</p>
<p><strong>Output format:</strong>
</p>
<p>Output the required answer on a new line.</p>
<p><br>
</p>
<p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>
<p>1 ≤ <strong>T</strong> ≤ 10^6</p>
<p>1 ≤ <strong>N</strong> ≤ 10^7</p>
<p></p>
<p></p>
<p></p></div></div><div class="less-margin-2 input-output-container"><div class="input-output right-border"><div class="form-label"><div class="weight-600 less-margin-right light float-left small">Sample Input</div><div class="input-output-opt float-right"><a href="https://he-s3-ap-south-1.s3.amazonaws.com/media/hackathon/january-long18/problems/688f8d8afa0711e7.txt?X-Amz-Algorithm=AWS4-HMAC-SHA256&amp;X-Amz-Credential=AKIA6I2ISGOYMPJGUFGY%2F20260407%2Fap-south-1%2Fs3%2Faws4_request&amp;X-Amz-Date=20260407T073037Z&amp;X-Amz-Expires=3600&amp;X-Amz-SignedHeaders=host&amp;X-Amz-Signature=09e4b60a09f4e7f39b47aadc7c760fe0400248cab610d3d518470e6e2b0eeae2" class="track-problem-sample-input tool-tip" title="Download" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><i class="fa fa-link"></i></a></div><div class="clear"></div></div><div class="dark"><pre class="word-spacing-0">2
